// OmniFlow batch 223 - Secrets vault: provider keys, tokens and webhook secrets are stored encrypted at rest.
//
// Run from the WEBSITE repo root (the bot root - the folder that contains OmniFlow-Control-Plane/):
//     node secrets_vault_223.mjs
// Needs batch 221 (kb_ocr_221.mjs) applied first. Safe to run twice (second run says "already"). Old copies are kept as *.pre_223.bak.
//
// What it does:
//  * Control Plane: portal_vault.py (new) - AES-256-GCM with a key that lives ONLY in the env (OF_SECRETS_KEY,
//    32+ characters). Stored format ofv1:<key id>:<data>. Reading still accepts old plaintext rows, so nothing
//    breaks before or after the key is set; with no key the CP behaves exactly as today (fail-soft).
//    Sealed on save, opened on load: platform provider keys (Admin -> Integrations), Instagram app secret +
//    access token, WATI token, catalog sync keys, courier keys (settings + providers), payment password/salt,
//    webhook signing secrets. Instagram verify_token stays plain (webhook lookup needs it).
//    platform_settings.py also commits its first-use table creation (fixes the first admin save on a fresh DB).
//    admin_providers.py - GET /api/v1/admin/security/vault (counts only, never values) and
//    POST /api/v1/admin/security/vault/migrate (encrypts legacy plaintext rows and re-seals rows made with an old key;
//    audited as security.vault_migrated). requirements.txt gets cryptography>=42.
//  * Website: Admin -> Integrations -> "Secrets encryption" card: status, per-area counts, "Encrypt stored secrets",
//    and "Generate a key" (made in the browser, never sent anywhere).
//  * Tests: tools/cp-testrig/test_vault.py (77 checks, incl. a real PostgreSQL run when pgserver is installed);
//    test_app_boot.py allows cryptography only lazily inside portal_vault.py.
//
// Setup (Control Plane env on Vercel):
//   1. OF_SECRETS_KEY = a random value of 32+ characters (the card's "Generate a key" makes one). Keep a copy in
//      your password manager - if it is lost, encrypted credentials must be re-entered.
//   2. Redeploy the CP, then Admin -> Integrations -> Secrets encryption -> "Encrypt stored secrets".
//   Rotation: set OF_SECRETS_KEY_OLD = the current key, OF_SECRETS_KEY = the new key, redeploy, press Encrypt again,
//   then remove OF_SECRETS_KEY_OLD. Optional: OF_VAULT_MIGRATE_MAX=5000 (rows per press).
// After running: CP  git add OmniFlow-Control-Plane... commit, push (Vercel installs cryptography);
//                website  git add -A, commit, push.
